Definitely has.

Example.
smela (experimental gismu), rutrprunu and birkoku are the synonyms.

Look at http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/natlang/en/apricot


But let's open xml export. The only record there is


<nlword word="apricot" valsi="smela" />



As for etymology it's fields are not exported.
http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/dict/smela has etymology filled in.


Let's look into xml export. What can we see ?
<valsi unofficial="true" word="smela" type="experimental 
gismu"><definition>$x_1$ is a plum/peach/cherry/apricot/almond/sloe [fruit] 
(genus Prunus) of species/variety $x_2lt;/definition><notes>{zirsmela} for 
plum, {xunsmela} for cherry, {najysmela} for peach, {pelsmela} for apricot, 
{ri'onsmela} for almond, {blasmela} for sloe.
Cf. {rutrprunu}, {ricrprunu}, {flaume}, {persika}, {rutrceraso}, {birkoku}, 
{frambesi}, {fragari}, {plise}, {perli}, {rozgu}</notes></valsi>


So no examples, etymology, vote information and discussion fields are 
present in xml export.

